Subject: [PATCH] compose: keep the profile when no GPU cluster fits the host

When no GPU cluster matches the host's graphics backend, the GPU values
come from the host and every other part of the profile is still
composed: timezone, locale, fonts, screen, cores, memory, media devices
and voices. The explain report records the gap. A GPU cluster pinned
with --fingerprint-anchor on a different backend is honored, and the
report notes that its extension list shrinks to what the host supports.

--- a/base/apostate/compose.cc
+++ b/base/apostate/compose.cc
@@ -485,28 +485,59 @@
     }
 
     if (servable.empty()) {
